SUMMARY:RegenAll + PCA&D: (Mini) Enviro-Zine Making 101: Grades 7 - 10
DESCRIPTION:In 2026\, RegenAll’s Youth Climate Art Exhibition will be a pre-event component of RegenAll’s Annual Climate Summit. Students from around the county will have the opportunity to express their vision of a thriving\, resilient\, and sustainable “green future” to promote creative and hopeful thinking for the next generation. We hope that their work will inspire decision-makers\, lawmakers\, and community members to see a better future for our shared environment. The exhibition will be held November 8 – 15 at Pennsylvania College of Art & Design’s Welcome Center (241 N. Prince Street\, Lancaster\, PA ) with an opening reception on Friday\, November 13\, 2026 from 5 – 7:30 pm.  \n\n\n\nOne way for young community members to submit work is in one of our free workshops held at PCA&D! Join us! This is a mini-zine making class for students in grades 7-10. This class will cover how to make an 8-page mini-zine and its many uses. The main goal of this class is to understand what goes into making a mini-zine and how they can be used as a tool for communicating ideas and opinions through art. In addition to mini-zine production\, students will learn mixed-media techniques; they will first brainstorm ideas for their zines and create a hard copy by collaging from recycled magazines and hand-drawn illustrations. Then\, once they are done with their hard copy\, they will learn how to copy and fold their zines. Walking away with 6 mini zines with their idea of a more environmentally conscious future. Instructor: Laurence Jacoby Saturday\, October 17 10 AM – 12 PM \n\n\n\n\n    Learn More
URL:https://figlancaster.com/event/regenall-pcad-mini-enviro-zine-making-101-grades-7-10/
LOCATION:Pennsylvania College of Art & Design – Center for Creative Exploration\, 204 North Prince Street\, Lancaster\, Pennsylvania\, 17603\, United States
CATEGORIES:Education & Classes
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://fig.guide/content/uploads/sites/3/2026/09/2.avif
ORGANIZER;CN="Pennsylvania College of Art & Design - Center for Creative Exploration":MAILTO:ce@pcad.edu
END:VEVENT
