SUMMARY:Beginning Colored Pencils: Grades 4-6 at PCA&D
DESCRIPTION:In this introductory workshop\, students in grades 4-6 will learn a variety of colored pencil techniques. These include stippling\, hatching\, scumbling and more! They will learn to blend and layer colors to create a vibrant drawing. This class has a lot of guidance and demonstration followed by time to practice. \n            \n        \n                \n            \n                \n                \n    Register Now
URL:https://figlancaster.com/event/beginning-colored-pencils-grades-4-6-at-pcad/
LOCATION:Pennsylvania College of Art & Design – Center for Creative Exploration\, 204 North Prince Street\, Lancaster\, Pennsylvania\, 17603\, United States
